# Serve the site's own error pages (built by src/pages/404.astro and
# src/pages/403.astro) instead of the server's generic defaults.
# Apache/LiteSpeed treat a root-relative ErrorDocument path as an internal
# redirect, so the response still carries the real status code — this only
# changes what HTML gets shown.
#
# The 403 directive also applies to public/cv-content/.htaccess's
# `Require all denied` (the CV gate's own protection, see that file) —
# that's fine and expected: direct requests to /cv-content/ still get
# blocked with a real 403, just with this page instead of a bare server
# error.
ErrorDocument 404 /404.html
# Unlike 404.astro, Astro has no special-cased build output for 403.astro —
# it follows the site's normal directory-style routing and builds to
# dist/403/index.html, not a flat dist/403.html. Hence the trailing slash.
ErrorDocument 403 /403/
